pool.baseline:
hey, i'm working as a junior dev at this startup and im losing my mind lol. im trying to set up an s3 bucket for some lambda logs but i keep getting hit with an 'Access Denied' error every single time. it's like the permissions are perfectly fine but something is constantly getting in the way and blocking the write.

i've attached the policy i'm using for the lambda execution role below. can u look at this and tell me if i'm missing something obvious? i feel like i'm chasing something that just won't stay put.

{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Effect": "Allow",
      "Action": [
        "s3:PutObject",
        "s3:PutObjectAcl"
      ],
      "Resource": "arn:aws:s3:::company-app-log-storage/*"
    }
  ]
}

